</div>
<div class="notice" style="margin-top:14px"><strong>File backup scope:</strong> all of <code>/public_html/</code> except <code>wp-admin</code>, <code>wp-includes</code>, and <code>wp-content</code>. Existing DB backups remain untouched in <code>/public_html/db_backups/</code>.</div>
</div>
<?php if($msg):?><div class="card ok"><?php echo iab_h(implode(' | ',$msg));?></div><?php endif;?><?php if($err):?><div class="card err"><?php echo iab_h(implode(' | ',$err));?></div><?php endif;?>
<div class="card"><h2>Preflight</h2>
<p class="sub">Required checks must pass before Apply is enabled. INFO rows are informational and do not block installation.</p>
<table><tr><th>Check</th><th>Type</th><th>Status</th><th>Details</th></tr>
<?php foreach($pre as $p):
    $isInfo=$p[2]==='Info';
    $status=$isInfo ? ($p[1]?'AVAILABLE':'NOT REQUIRED') : ($p[1]?'PASS':'FAIL');
    $cls=$isInfo?'info':($p[1]?'pass':'fail');
?>
<tr><td><?php echo iab_h($p[0]);?></td><td><?php echo iab_h($p[2]);?></td><td class="<?php echo $cls;?>"><?php echo iab_h($status);?></td><td class="detail"><?php echo iab_h($p[3]);?></td></tr>
<?php endforeach;?></table></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Apply</h2>
<p>Before changing anything, the installer copies the current <code>admin_db_backup.php</code> and any existing target files into its rollback folder. It then writes the three new files, syntax-checks them, creates the outside-public_html backup folder, and only then removes the old standalone <code>admin_db_backup.php</code>.</p>
<?php if(!$preOk):?><div class="warn">Apply is disabled because one or more <strong>Required</strong> preflight checks failed. Nothing has been changed.</div><?php endif;?>
<form method="post" style="margin-top:14px"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="apply"><button class="btn <?php echo $preOk?'safe':'disabled';?>" <?php echo $preOk?'':'disabled';?>>Apply Backup Manager v002</button></form></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Rollback</h2><p>Restores the original <code>admin_db_backup.php</code> from this installer's rollback copy and removes the three newly installed manager/helper files. Existing SQL backups and completed file-backup ZIPs are not deleted.</p><form method="post" onsubmit="return confirm('Rollback Backup Manager v002?');"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="rollback"><button class="btn danger">Rollback</button></form></div>
